MediaBox: every deinterlaced field at its own time, from the key frame on.

Measured 2026-11-06 on the Plus (MPP 0986d01, IEP2, deinterlace mode) with
the streams in tests/mpp, 576i whose every field shows its own time (a bar
that moves on every field), and on 1080i50 DVB-S2 (vproc_debug=0xc2):

  1. A picture the decoder marks discard -- an open GOP's leading B
     pictures, whose references came before decoding started -- went into
     the deinterlacer's history. The first good frame after the key frame
     was deinterlaced against them; its two pictures came out timed before
     the key frame or marked in error and were dropped. 3 of 13 openings.
  2. After the key frame's first field (I1O1T) the next frame put out
     nothing ("Wait for next frame"), and I5O2 started with the second
     frame's fields: the key frame's second field was never shown.
  3. I5O2 gives the centre frame's (prev0's) two fields but timed them half
     a frame early, the first between prev1 and prev0: every picture showed
     what was 20 ms after its timestamp, which hid 2 as an even cadence and
     put the picture 20 ms ahead of the sound on every interlaced stream.
  4. After a transport loss the pictures decoded from a lost reference
     (errinfo) went into the history too: the key frame that ends the loss
     was deinterlaced against them, its pictures marked in error and
     dropped -- both of its fields, 40 ms, after every loss (a 480 ms hole
     on TRT 1 and in tests/mpp/open-gop-576i-bar-hole.ts).
  5. With 3 fixed, a second field timed halfway to the next frame came out
     80 ms late where the next frame was no neighbour: at a loss on TRT 1
     the decoder put out POC 48 before POC 40, and at another only every
     other frame (0, 4, 8, 16), evenly apart, twice as far.

Now a discarded picture comes out untouched (gstmppdec and FFmpeg drop it)
and leaves the history as it was; a picture in error comes out untouched
and ends the history, the next good one starting it as a stream's first
does; the first frame's second field comes out from that field alone
(I1O1B, or I1O1T bottom field first) half a frame after the first; I5O2's
pictures carry prev0's time and the time half a frame on, half a frame
the least that three frames evenly apart measured. The newest frame of the
history goes unshown when a picture in error ends it: next to the loss in
tests/mpp the decoder gave such a frame, unmarked, showing what was ten
fields before its time.
scripts/test-mpp-deinterlace.sh: without this patch the opening has 47
pictures, the key frame's second field missing and each picture one field
ahead of its time, and after the loss the key frame's fields are missing;
with it the opening has 50 pictures, fields 28 to 77, and after the loss
every field from the key frame's first, each at its own time. Taking out
any one of 1-4 fails it; 5 is seen on the broadcast only.

